        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-10-03T16:12:08.062Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think the quintessential example of a game mechanic decision being made wrong for story reasons is the Elemental Redistributor in Baron Blade’s deck.  He has two copies of a card that most heroes can completely ignore, just because he needed to have it in case of fighting Absolute Zero, who isn’t even his nemesis, just an ally thereof.  It should be a single card, and or should be combined with some other card like the Flesh Repair Nanites.</p>\n<p>A thing they couldn’t talk about in this episode, because they don’t own the character, but which absolutely fits, is the Cauldron hero Impact and his gravity powers, which are almost entirely defined as Infernal damage.  If you’re falling or being crushed, that’s going to have a lot of the same look and feel as the dark powers commanded by Nightmist, who doesn’t do fire, or Gloomweaver, who does eldritch green fire that probably mostly doesn’t burn so much as rot and fester.  Apostate blurs those lines on purpose, just as Fanatic blurs the line between fire or energy and radiant.  But in general, Infernal is anything negative and corruptive that isn’t better represented by like toxic radiation or the like.</p>\n<p>They don’t admit it, but because they didn’t conceptualize Spite until almost a year after the Wraith, I would bet good money that they originally had vague thoughts of what would become the Chairman as being the eventual Wraith nemesis, and then they later invented Mr Fixer to have a closer relationship with Chairman, or perhaps Operative vs Fixer was originally a separate villain deck and story from Chairman vs Wraith.  But luckily they changed their mind and created the best, most awesomely dynamic to fight, totally not gross or creepy at all character to be Wraith’s archenemy.  Yaaaay.</p>\n<p>Speaking of villains, I wouldn’t call Iron Legacy the hardest.  Chairman is much worse.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group quote-modified\" data-username=\"MigrantP\" data-post=\"20\" data-topic=\"18128\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/48/1921_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MigrantP:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That’s been on our idea list for a long time. It would be a lot of work. Maybe someday!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think doing that is within the possibility of modern AI, though it would take a lot of trial and error to get it right.</p>",
