      {
        "id": 263938,
        "name": "",
        "username": "LonelyMan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-10-03T21:57:58.252Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I agree it probably shouldn’t be integrated fully.  Too much chance of cross contamination.  But I think if an AI were trained on all the art Adam ever did, and also on how to read Handelabra logs, you could probably code together a generator that turns the log into a comic.  I wouldn’t advise crossing the streams much more than that.</p>\n<p>Speaking of things C&amp;A will never admit, I remain firmly convinced that Benchmark is basically just version 2.0 of Bunker, who is the most clearly “off” of the core set heroes.  I think it’s telling that in both the Miss Information story and the Omnitron animated series story, and probably any other story you’d ever do about Wager Master or the like doing a similar thing to the heroes, you end up with all the other heroes having a challenge that cuts to the quick of who they are and forces them to adapt, but in Bunker’s case it’s just that the Bunker suit stops working and it’s just Tyler Vance with a sidearm, not in any way being the superhero Bunker anymore.  Compare that with Benchmark losing control of his suit and having to trash it himself, then fighting Revenant with his suit in pieces, it’s just a much better story, and makes it seem that Randall Butler is still Benchmark even with only like 20% of the suit, while Bunker even in the full suit seems out of place among superheroes.</p>",
