      {
        "id": 263941,
        "name": "FrivYeti",
        "username": "FrivYeti",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/frivyeti/{size}/1919_2.png",
        "created_at": "2025-10-03T23:57:33.677Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Of course it’s not going to replace Adam. AI isn’t going to replace anyone except the poor workers whose bosses are too stupid and green-blinded to recognize that their miracle tool is snake oil. A bunch of churned-out pablum vaguely in the shape of a Sentinel Comics issue isn’t going to replace his ideas, or the game, or the discussions that fans have or the stories that they imagine when they play. It won’t replace anything. It has no value whatsoever except to waste the time of the people reading.</p>\n<p>It’s depressing because it’s an <em>insult</em>. To Adam, and to every other creative in the world. To say that we should feed his work into a drek machine to churn out reams and reams of meaningless slop, burning vast amounts of energy and enriching the worst elements of humanity in exchange for <em>nothing</em>.</p>\n<p>What’s depressing is the fact that there are people who <em>want that</em>. Who, with the literal <em>millions</em> of talented, skilled artists and writers out there producing amazing, beautiful, inspiring work, would rather turn to the sludge machine to produce content that vaguely reminds them of a property that they like, who want to spend the limited hours of their glorious existence just <em>consuming shit</em>.</p>\n<p>It’s awful. It’s disgusting. It legitimately and actually makes me grieve.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2025-10-03T23:57:33.677Z",
